                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Sun samples per hour. 1 is hourly; 10 gives a 6-minute step. An hour moves the sun ~15°, so against a sharp shadow edge an hourly step misses transitions — measured at 3.33 h of error on 245 sunlit point-hours, where a 6-minute step is 12.5× closer (docs/SUN_ANALYSIS.md). Cost is linear: 10 is 10× the rays.</item>
